#. world_info.csv: Orthodoxy
msgid "WORLD_INFO_ORTHODOXY_TITLE"
msgstr "Orthodoxy"

#. world_info.csv: The world's underlying standard realms, from we...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_REALM_DESC"
msgstr ""
"The world's underlying standard realms, from weak to strong, are Qi "
"Refinement, Foundation Establishment, Core Formation, and Nascent Soul. Each"
" realm has Early, Middle, and Late stages. Different traditions may use "
"aliases, but rules are calculated by this standard sequence."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_REALM_NAME"
msgstr "Realm"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_REALM_TITLE"
msgstr "Realm"

#. world_info.csv: Different regions have different effects; doing...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_REGION_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Different regions have different effects; doing the right thing in the right"
" region yields twice the result with half the effort."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_REGION_NAME"
msgstr "Region"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_REGION_TITLE"
msgstr "Region"

#. world_info.csv: Spirit roots are composed of five elements (Met...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_ROOT_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Spirit roots are composed of five elements (Metal, Wood, Water, Fire, "
"Earth), divided into Single, Dual, and Heavenly Spirit Roots. Five elements "
"interaction: Metal overcomes Wood, Wood overcomes Earth, Earth overcomes "
"Water, Water overcomes Fire, Fire overcomes Metal. Heavenly Spirit Root "
"contains all five elements and has an extra bonus during breakthrough. "
"Cultivation efficiency is highest in regions matching one's own spirit root "
"attribute."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_ROOT_NAME"
msgstr "Spirit Root"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_ROOT_TITLE"
msgstr "Spirit Root"

#. world_info.csv: Secret realms open every few years. Entering a ...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_SECRET_REALM_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Secret realms open every few years. Entering a secret realm may encounter "
"danger, but may also obtain high-level artifacts and techniques."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SECRET_REALM_NAME"
msgstr "Secret Realm"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SECRET_REALM_TITLE"
msgstr "Secret Realm"

#. world_info.csv: A shelter for cultivators. Joining a sect allow...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_SECT_DESC"
msgstr ""
"A shelter for cultivators. Joining a sect allows learning unique techniques "
"and gaining protection from fellow disciples; rogue cultivators are free but"
" lack resources."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SECT_NAME"
msgstr "Sect"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SECT_TITLE"
msgstr "Sect"

#. world_info.csv: In city regions, you can buy Qi Refinement-grad...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_SHOPPING_DESC"
msgstr ""
"In city regions, you can buy Qi Refinement-grade elixirs and weapons. "
"Purchased elixirs are consumed immediately to strengthen the character; "
"purchased weapons can switch the character to a more suitable weapon type."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SHOPPING_NAME"
msgstr "Shopping"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SHOPPING_TITLE"
msgstr "Shopping"

#. world_info.csv: The common currency of the cultivation world. C...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_SPIRIT_STONE_DESC"
msgstr ""
"The common currency of the cultivation world. Can be used to buy artifacts "
"and elixirs, obtained through gathering, trading, or plundering."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SPIRIT_STONE_NAME"
msgstr "Spirit Stone"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_SPIRIT_STONE_TITLE"
msgstr "Spirit Stone"

#. world_info.csv: The world undergoes celestial changes (such as ...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_WORLD_QI_DESC"
msgstr ""
"The world undergoes celestial changes (such as Qi Tides) every few years, "
"affecting character abilities."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_WORLD_QI_NAME"
msgstr "World Qi"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_WORLD_QI_TITLE"
msgstr "World Qi"

#. world_info.csv: The cultivation world features the Heaven, Eart...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_RANKING_DESC"
msgstr ""
"The cultivation world features the Heaven, Earth, and Human Rankings, as "
"well as the Sect Ranking. The three personal rankings are grouped by "
"equivalent standard realm: Heaven records Nascent Soul-tier experts, Earth "
"records Core Formation-tier experts, and Human records Foundation "
"Establishment-tier experts. The Sect Ranking ranks sects by total power."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_RANKING_NAME"
msgstr "Ranking"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_RANKING_TITLE"
msgstr "Ranking"

#. world_info.csv: Mortal dynasties rule the realm, maintaining wo...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_DYNASTY_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Mortal dynasties rule the realm, maintaining worldly order and borders. "
"Emperors live no longer than ordinary mortals, and when one dies, a new "
"emperor succeeds to the throne."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_DYNASTY_NAME"
msgstr "Dynasty"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_DYNASTY_TITLE"
msgstr "Dynasty"

#. world_info.csv: Cultivators may govern for the imperial court, ...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_OFFICIAL_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Cultivators may govern for the imperial court, building court reputation and"
" receiving salary. With enough reputation they can be promoted; the higher "
"the office, the greater the salary and luck. If they neglect governance for "
"too long, their reputation will gradually decline."

msgid "WORLD_INFO_OFFICIAL_NAME"
msgstr "Official Rank"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_OFFICIAL_TITLE"
msgstr "Official Rank"

#. world_info.csv: The same cultivation ranks have different names in each
#. tradition.
msgid "WORLD_INFO_CULTIVATION_ALIAS_DESC"
msgstr ""
"The same cultivation ranks have different names in each tradition: Daoists "
"and rogue cultivators use Qi Refinement, Foundation Establishment, Core "
"Formation, and Nascent Soul; martial cultivators use Body Tempering, Tendon-"
"Tempering, Martial Master, and Martial Saint; Confucian cultivators use "
"Vital Qi Cultivation, Principle Illumination, Mandate Establishment, and "
"Great Scholar; Buddhist cultivators use Novice Monk, Monk, Arhat, and "
"Bodhisattva; yao cultivators use Spirit Awakening, Form Transformation, "
"Demon Core, and Demon King. These names map to the same underlying realm "
"sequence; they change narrative and interface wording, but not breakthrough,"
" power, lifespan, item grade, or other rules."

#. world_info.csv: Realm Aliases
msgid "WORLD_INFO_CULTIVATION_ALIAS_NAME"
msgstr "Realm Aliases"

#. world_info.csv: Realm Aliases
msgid "WORLD_INFO_CULTIVATION_ALIAS_TITLE"
msgstr "Realm Aliases"

#. world_info.csv: Gu arts require a cultivator to carry a Gu tool...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_GU_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Gu arts require a cultivator to carry a Gu tool and have the ability to "
"inflict Gu before applying it to an observable target. Different Gu act in "
"different ways: Mind-Sinking Gu subtly shifts relationships, Blood-Devouring"
" Gu periodically damages life, while Essence-Eroding Gu and Heart-"
"Disordering Gu disturb cultivation. Inflicting Gu has a success rate "
"affected by the tool, the caster's bonuses, and the target's Gu resistance; "
"failure may be detected and harm the relationship."

#. world_info.csv:
msgid "WORLD_INFO_GU_NAME"
msgstr "Gu"

#. world_info.csv: Gu
msgid "WORLD_INFO_GU_TITLE"
msgstr "Gu"

#. world_info.csv: Formations require a cultivator to carry a form...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_FORMATION_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Formations require a cultivator to carry a formation disk and have "
"formation-setting ability before placing a temporary regional effect at the "
"current location. Different formations suit different regions: cultivation "
"grounds and sect regions can hold spirit-gathering, mountain-guarding, "
"clarity, and similar arrays; cities can hold healing arrays; mines, herb "
"fields, and beast domains can hold vein-seeking, wood-growth, and beast-"
"driving arrays. Formations consume spirit stones and expire after their "
"duration ends."

#. world_info.csv:
msgid "WORLD_INFO_FORMATION_NAME"
msgstr "Formations"

#. world_info.csv: Formations
msgid "WORLD_INFO_FORMATION_TITLE"
msgstr "Formations"

#. world_info.csv: Cultivators may occasionally feel a sudden stir...
msgid "WORLD_INFO_OPPORTUNITY_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Cultivators may occasionally feel a sudden stir of fate, sensing that a "
"person or place is tied to their own opportunity. If they follow the sense, "
"they may gain treasure or a boon, return empty-handed, or meet danger; if "
"they delay too long, the opportunity fades away."

#. world_info.csv:
msgid "WORLD_INFO_OPPORTUNITY_NAME"
msgstr "Opportunity"

#. world_info.csv: Opportunity
msgid "WORLD_INFO_OPPORTUNITY_TITLE"
msgstr "Opportunity"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_RACE_TITLE"
msgstr "Race"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_RACE_NAME"
msgstr "Race"

msgid "WORLD_INFO_RACE_DESC"
msgstr ""
"The world contains both human and yao cultivators. Yao include fox, wolf, "
"bird, snake, turtle, and other races, each with different instincts: foxes "
"are clever and sly, wolves are fierce hunters, birds excel at migration and "
"scouting, snakes are patient and venomous, and turtles are long-lived and "
"defensive. Yao can cultivate and join sects that accept them, but some sects"
" that emphasize human rites or Confucian order do not accept yao."
